From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koji Ishii <kojii@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:42:21 +0900
Subject: [icu] Fix usearch CE index overflow and FCD loop

Cherry-pick upstream ICU fixes for ICU-23568 (574e55d50531), ICU-22511
(75dec2921c73 and d76909c20d46), and ICU-23569 (3fa621389fc7).

Previously, CEIBuffer::get(), CEIBuffer::getPrevious(),
usearch_search(), and usearch_searchBackwards() tracked
collation-element indexes in int32_t, causing signed overflow and
negative ring-buffer subscripts past INT32_MAX processed collation
elements. In addition, FCDUTF16CollationIterator::previousCodePoint()
and FCDUIterCollationIterator::previousCodePoint() checked trailing
combining classes on raw UTF-16 trail surrogates, missing supplementary
characters with non-zero tccc and entering an infinite backtracking
loop.

Widen CEIBuffer and search collation-element indexes to int64_t, and
check paired lead surrogates via CollationFCD::hasTcccBefore() and
U16_IS_TRAIL() during backward FCD iteration.

Bug: 574025697
Test: blink_unittests --gtest_filter=TextSearcherIcuTest.*
Change-Id: I982b1d76cdbc03b2d357d53dba32ce49ef505c4c
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/deps/icu/+/8668040
Reviewed-by: Kent Tamura <tkent@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
The upstream change also refreshes the copies of these fixes stored under third_party/icu/patches/ (usearch_ceibuffer_64bit.patch, collation_fcd_tccc.patch), which are only consulted when ICU is re-rolled and whose diff-context lines carry trailing whitespace that Electron's patch lint rejects; those stored-patch hunks are not carried. The ICU source and test changes are carried verbatim.

